title: Elections to the National Assembly
subtitle: Germany votes on 19 January.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1919 and month = 1 and spartacist_uprising_done = 1 and crisis = 0
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
// historical results, 19 January 1919 (423 seats; the Centre and the BVP stood together)
Q.parliament_name = 'National Assembly';
Q.parliament_size = 423;
Q.spd_seats = 163; Q.zentrum_seats = 91; Q.ddp_seats = 75; Q.dnvp_seats = 44;
Q.uspd_seats = 22; Q.dvp_seats = 19; Q.bvp_seats = 0; Q.nsdap_seats = 0;
!}

= Elections to the National Assembly

[? if luxemburg_alive = 0 : Four days after the murders of 15 January, ?][? if luxemburg_alive = 1 and liebknecht_alive = 0 : Four days after the murder of Liebknecht, ?][? if luxemburg_alive = 1 and liebknecht_alive = 1 : Four days after the manhunt of 15 January, ?] Germany votes for a National Assembly that will write the new constitution. It is the first national election in which women can vote. Ebert's party expects to win it outright.

Our founding congress voted by 62 to 23 to boycott it, against the Zentrale. [? if luxemburg_alive = 1 : Luxemburg still thinks the boycott is a mistake: the Assembly is a fortress of the counter-revolution, and we should storm it from inside, as a platform. ?][? if luxemburg_alive = 0 : Luxemburg argued that we must use even the Assembly as a platform. She is dead, and her argument is now a question of loyalty to her memory. ?] The lists close in days.

- @boycott: Respect the congress and boycott the election.
- @active: Turn the boycott into a day of protest.
- @candidates: Overrule the congress and stand candidates where we can.
- @vote_uspd: Tell workers to vote for the USPD.

@boycott
subtitle: The Left Radicals' line, and the congress's decision. The Zentrale obeys.
on-arrival: ultraleft_satisfaction += 6; luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 4; worker_support -= 2; lean_ultraleft += 2; election_boycott = 1

Our posters call on workers to stay away. Most vote anyway, for the SPD and the Independents.

@active
subtitle: The Left's version: demonstrations at the polling stations. Militant, and dangerous.
on-arrival: ultraleft_satisfaction += 4; offensive_satisfaction += 6; militancy += 6; repression += 6; worker_support -= 3; lean_offensive += 2; lean_ultraleft += 1; election_boycott = 1

Our marchers shout down speakers outside the polling stations in Neukölln and Hamborn. The police make arrests, and the voters step round them.

@candidates
subtitle: [? if lock_elections = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Spartacist position. Overruling a congress costs Unity too, and it is very late to register lists.
choose-if: lock_elections < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids taking part in bourgeois elections.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_elections == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.unity -= 8;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction -= 10;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 6;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 4;
Q.worker_support += 4;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
Q.lean_ultraleft -= 2;
Q.election_boycott = 0;
// a few seats, taken mostly from the Independents
Q.kpd_seats = Q.luxemburg_alive ? 4 : 2;
Q.uspd_seats -= Q.kpd_seats - 1;
Q.spd_seats -= 1;
!}

Our lists appear in Berlin, Saxony and a handful of other constituencies. We win [+ kpd_seats +] seats. A principle has been set: the Zentrale, not the congress, has the last word. The districts will remember.

@vote_uspd
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Right's answer. Helps the Independents; the Left Radicals are appalled.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids any support for social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.uspd_relation += 12;
Q.uspd_seats += 2;
Q.spd_seats -= 2;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction -= 10;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 6;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
Q.election_boycott = 1;
!}

The Independents gain votes in the workers' districts, and they know whom to thank. Officially, the party still boycotts.
